th, wisdom, ingenious ideas, wit, intelligence, flourishing... love of the guiding star in the Universe from which all flourishing becomes possible. And, the feeling is impatience with a less-than-ideal status quo, impatience with pettiness and small talk, impatience with small-minded others, with lack of questioning. Impatience with confident ignorance, with minds that think they know it all when they know very little. Impatience with a lot of noise from the Social layer, distraction that drives Q2I to seek the solitude of their own minds. \n\nAnd as a consequence of that solitude, loneliness is a big part of Q2I\u0027s feeling. It\u0027s not that they don\u0027t want to be with other people so much as they don\u0027t want to be distracted from the truth and goodness Up above by other people. They don\u0027t want to be distracted by the conversations of tribes on the deck of the ship when they need to fix their gaze above that horizontal plane at the guiding star at the top of the vertical axis.\n\nWhat does that look like? Well... Q2I might avoid eye contact with others. They might want to observe others but not interact with them. They\u0027d have a tendency to close their eyes and think inward, or watch other people unobtrusively, not wanting anyone to know that they\u0027re observing and studying their patterns. They would be loners, introverts, wallflowers, feeling in this world but not *of* this world. \"I\u0027m just a non-human observer, like a space alien viewing from a very distant perspective. I\u0027m studying this species, but I don\u0027t feel as if I belong to this species. I study things not as a human, but as a universal consciousness that studies humans.\"\n\nOkay, but what does that *look* like! Hmm... closed eyes, or not looking directly at other people but instead straight up at the patterns of the Universal layer revealed at the top of the vertical axis where all understandings of truth and goodness converge. The picture could be one of lookin