        "text": " the side, scanning for social cues, desperately asking, \"Am I fitting in? Do they approve? Am I saying the right thing?\"\n"
      }, {
        "text": "*   **The Hands**: The **\"Sideways Open Hand.\"** Open and receptive, but turned horizontally, not upward"
      }, {
        "text": ". It is the hand waiting to see which way the wind of social approval will blow, ready to conform to whatever is"
      }, {
        "text": " demanded.\n*   **The Posture**: The forced smile, the nodding agreement, the body that mirrors the group"
      }, {
        "text": " while the soul recoils. There is often a visible tension—the shoulders slightly raised, the jaw tight—the body holding"
      }, {
        "text": " what the mind refuses to speak. It is the tragicomic image of the cartoon dog sitting in a burning room, saying,"
